<title>FRANCE: Lyonnaise seeks 15 pct return in Manila.</title>
<headline>Lyonnaise seeks 15 pct return in Manila.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>French utilities company Lyonnaise des Eaux expects a 15 percent return on its investment in a 25-year Philippine water contract, deputy chairman Guy de Panafieu said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Lyonnaise and its local partner Benpres Holdings Corp won the bidding for supplying fresh water and water treatment for Manila's west zone, which has seven million inhabitants.</p>
<p>Investment needs are expected to run to between $2.5-4 billion over the contract period and average annual turnover will be $200 million in the first 10 years.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
